p this  walk-on surprise in the movie of shazam  they had to use a stand-in and keep his  face covered but  ignoring all this stupid  behind-the-scenes drama this man of  steel cameo is still super fun  exactly the joyous fan service that  makes shazam so  great but let's now move on to the first  of the two post-credits scenes we see dr  thaddeus savannah mark strong in his  cramped prison cell  mumbling and madly scribbling the  ancient seven symbols as a way to try to  regain his magic  but of course it doesn't work perhaps  because shazam broke the wizard's staff  after sharing powers with the other kids  in his family savannah's pencil or  whatever he's using snaps and he screams  and he pounds on the wall  but then a voice calls out to him  hahahaha primitive simples  you walking talking monkeys with your  cave drawings  you assume there's only one way to gain  magic no  no no there are more ways than the mind  can imagine  and after looking around confused  savannah finally sees the voices coming  from a little worm on the windowsill  it's got a voice translator around its  neck i guess worms are kind of  all neck savannah asks what in god's  name and the worm cuts them off saying  i am the gods doctor not the other way  around  oh what fun we're about to have together  the seven realms are about to be ours  so i know some of you were like what so  this is mr mind  a dc villain and well known foe to  shazam  captain marvel he's also known as  captain marvel originally in the comics  in mr mind leads the monster society of  evil  not known for its subtlety but hey it's  comics mr mind is telepathic  and has mind control based powers which  makes the voice translator kind of  redundant but  so is the name monster society of evil  and again comics mr mind actually showed  up earlier in the film as an easter egg  trapped in an encasement in the rock of  eternity  but later when savannah finds the place  and gains the power of the seven deadly  sins the encasement is shown again  shattered and empty now i'm gonna go  deeper into why mr mine's appearance  could be important for the future of the  dceu but before i continue big thanks to  rage shadow legends for sponsoring this  video  read shadow legends is an awesome mobile  game probably the most immersive  experience you will find on a smart  device  honestly we should be comparing it to  the biggest pc and console titles but  this game is totally free  raid has all the features that you'd  expect from a brand new rpg title  an amazing storyline awesome 3d graphics  giant boss fights pvp battles  and hundreds of champions to collect and  customize guys i never expected to get  this level performance out of a mobile  game  just look how crazy the level of detail  is on these champions  geez uh i i would tell her to cover  herself up some more but  those are um skull earrings and i  believe they're human size  raid is getting big real fast so jump on  this to get a huge head start  there's also a special launch tournament  coming up with crazy in-game prizes and  real life physical prize packs  so go down to the description and  download raid only through our links to  get 50 000 silver immediately  and a free epic champion as part of the  new player program courtesy of the  developer team  see you there okay back to mr mind in  the shazam post credits scene mr mine  was first introduced as a super  intelligent alien worm from venus who  was attracted to earth's radio signals  and later on his monster's society of  evil was one of the earliest times in  comics that  past villains band together along with  mr mind on the team there was  dummy and mr who and ramulus it was kind  of goofy but it did lay the groundwork  for future entities like the legion of  doom also you could say the sinister six  or maybe even the suicide squad now in  the scene notice that mr mine mentions  the seven realms  this could indicate that mr mind is  being adapted from the more recent dc  comics in which he's  maximum his mind and he attempts to  control the power of the seven magic  lands  there's the earth lands the fun lands  the game lands the dark lands the  monster lands  the wazanderlands and the wildlands  where mr mine comes from by establishing  these seven realms mr mind is broadening  the dc cinematic universe  in the kind of way that movies like thor  did for the mcu with its nine realms  or another analogy could be doctor  strange with the way it introduced a  multiverse of various dimensions  accessed through magic mr mine could  also be the gateway to how black adam  could join this universe  black adam is shazam's primary  antagonist and in the new 52 relaunch  dr savannah is the one to reawaken black  adam from his tomb  black adam actually cameoed as a little  easter egg earlier on as a projection  and that projection did kind of look  like dwayne the rock johnson who's going  to be playing him in a future film  so by expanding shazam's world to these  seven realms  it's all but certain that black adam  will probably be part of this universe  and that brings us to the final  post-credits scene of shazam a jokey  stinger that rolls at the very end of  the credits shazam and freddy are back  testing powers including talking to fish  he says this to his goldfish  don't beat yourself up little buddy  you're gonna find someone  yeah i'm sure because there's plenty of  fish in the sea  now this scene might have been cut from  the power testing montage earlier in the  movie  because you may remember it from one of  the trailers i can't talk to fish what  could we do with that that's cool maybe  uh command a  an army of billions in the ocean oh yeah  and in this scene it holds on shazam a  bit longer as he says  well that's not that cool and you  probably noticed that freddie's wearing  one of his many justice league hero  shirts showing the aquaman logo  with this whole final stinger being  another shout out to the dceu  and i look forward to re-watching shazam  to catch all of the easter eggs because  boy oh boy there were a lot of them so  comment down below with your favorite  moment from shazam and follow me on  instagram and twitter at eavos and  subscribe to new rockstars for deep  dives and all the stuff you love and for  those of you so desperate to see  superman's face in that final shot fine  look here he is  look see there's no head that's why  freddie freeman screamed  are you happy now  [Music]  you

